#[$in title:["Numbers"]]
#[$in description:["Numeric types, literals, operators and checked arithmetic in Moth."]]
#[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

#[navbar]
#[sidebar]
init_docs_sidebar()!
#[section, $md:
    # Numbers

    Moth's bounded numeric types name exact widths and precisions. Unconstrained
    whole-number values default to `I32`, while decimal/exponent values default
    to `F64`. These defaults do not impose arithmetic minimums: equal `I8`,
    `U8` and `F16` operands keep their narrow result type.

    Numeric literals retain their origin while body-local constraints resolve
    them. Operators check or round at their selected result type, including
    every `F16` operation. See the Progress matrix for current compiler and
    backend support: @../progress (Progress).
]

